  "correct_answer": [
    "A"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><img alt=\"\" src=\"assets\\st0166_5c34f1c6261a.png\" style=\"width: 418px; height: 150px;\" /></p><p>Due to the presence of two electron-withdrawing&nbsp;carbonyl group&nbsp;the methylene protons are very much acidic. The&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi></math>&nbsp;effect of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>COCH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;is more than&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><mi>COOMe</mi></math>. Hence, the acidic nature of acetyl acetone is more than rest of the two molecules.</p>"
